# Objective

Create a complete production-ready Rich Text CSS system for all HTML generated from CKEditor.

The generated CSS must be reusable, scalable, responsive, accessible, and should work for all pages that render CMS content.

The implementation MUST NOT break any existing UI or component styling.

Everything must be scoped under a wrapper class.

Example:

.editor-content

Never apply global styling directly to HTML tags.

Correct:

.editor-content h1 {}

Wrong:

h1 {}

--------------------------------------------------------

# Requirements

Cursor must:

- Analyze every HTML element CKEditor can generate.
- Generate CSS for ALL supported tags.
- Do not skip any tag.
- Do not leave TODO comments.
- Do not leave placeholder CSS.
- Every selector must have meaningful styling.

--------------------------------------------------------

# Scope

Everything must be inside:

.editor-content

Example

.editor-content h1 {}

.editor-content p {}

.editor-content table {}

Never style globally.

